@@ -96,7 +96,7 @@ Tickets have no order today. They should: every issue and raft gets a `rank:` (i
 - The z-nile app in Omarchy shows the same order, marks lost items, and reorders by drag and drop through `./zn rank`. *captured* (c0257)
 
 ### Claiming across hosts
-A worker claims an item by landing the status change on `origin/main`, as `status <id> preparing` and z-ready already do. The push is the lock: a lost race means taking the next item. Each step runs in its own worktree under `.worktree/` on the worker's host, and a worker pushes its layer branch after every commit, so a taker on any host recovers all committed work. The worker's identity (host, CLI, model) goes on its spend rows. *captured* (c0254) (the claim itself *exists*)
+A worker claims a raft (or an issue whose design it drafts) by landing the status change on `origin/main`, as `z-ready` and `status <id> preparing` already do. The push is the lock: a lost race means taking the next raft. The dispatcher asks `origin/main` before it takes a pick and after a claim step that failed, and an item another worker holds under a stamp that is not its own ends the run with exit 6 (`taken`), which the supervisor counts and answers by asking `./zn next` again at once; a rafting claim is the raft's claim, so two hosts never raft one issue. A `preparing` claim means a worker drafting the design for a person to approve. Each step runs in its own worktree under `.worktree/` on the worker's host, and a worker pushes its layer branch after every commit, and a prep branch too (`./zn commit` pushes the branch's own name, and exits 7 when the push is refused under a claim and 8 when it fails), so a taker on any host continues from all committed work and builds its own worktree from the pushed branch. A worker whose claim was taken over, or has ended, is told to stop and never pushes, finishes or restacks that branch again; its idle worktree on its own host is marked discarded by `./zn sync`, kept while the work lives or holds unrecovered files or commits, and removed once the work has ended (`./zn reap` lists what is left). A claim commit carries a `Worker:` trailer with the worker's host, CLI and model for every item it stamps, spend rows record the host, the CLI and the model of the step that spent them, and the board's card ("held by") and `./zn work status` show which worker holds what. *exists* (c0254) (the claim itself *exists*)
 - A worker that holds an item beats a heartbeat on it every 5 minutes, as a commit on a heartbeat branch, not on `main`; the branch is deleted when the heartbeat drops or the task completes. An item in progress whose heartbeat is stale is lost. *designed* (c0265)
 - Agents keep their claims alive without remembering to beat: the claim paths, every `./zn` command in a worktree, long commands and the dispatcher beat. *designed* (c0275)
 - A lost claim is taken over by the next worker as a normal claim, which resumes it and is recorded, and its old owner is refused and told: the takeover deletes the old heartbeat branch and creates a new one, so a worker that comes back learns it lost the claim. *designed* (c0274)
